NextBSD: fix LIBXML_VERSION in the CMake build (upstream #365).

Origin: upstream commit 94ac5e61f399759a5463c0505099222ed8f13a82
("CMakeLists.txt: Fix LIBXML_VERSION_NUMBER", Nick Wellnhofer,
2022-04-07, in 2.9.14), applied unchanged.

2.9.13's CMakeLists.txt pastes the version digits together with "0"
between them, so xmlversion.h said LIBXML_VERSION 209013 instead of
20913 (major * 10000 + minor * 100 + micro, as configure.ac computes it).
Code that compares LIBXML_VERSION then took 2.9.13 for something newer
than 2.12 (209013 >= 21200): WebKit picked the 2.12 const xmlError*
callback signature and failed to compile (nextbsd/nextbsd#740).

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -106,10 +106,13 @@
 	endif()
 endforeach()
 
-set(LIBXML_VERSION ${LIBXML_MAJOR_VERSION}0${LIBXML_MINOR_VERSION}0${LIBXML_MICRO_VERSION})
-set(LIBXML_VERSION_STRING "${LIBXML_VERSION}")
+set(LIBXML_VERSION ${VERSION})
 set(LIBXML_VERSION_EXTRA "")
-set(LIBXML_VERSION_NUMBER ${LIBXML_VERSION})
+math(EXPR LIBXML_VERSION_NUMBER "
+    ${LIBXML_MAJOR_VERSION} * 10000 +
+    ${LIBXML_MINOR_VERSION} * 100 +
+    ${LIBXML_MICRO_VERSION}
+")
 
 set(MODULE_EXTENSION "${CMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_SUFFIX}")
 
